\newlabel{sec:related}{{2}{2}{}{section.2}{}}
\newlabel{fig:arch}{{1}{3}{The substrate (7 layers, $d{=}256$, BPE-1024). Every mixing op is max/min-plus or a gather; the forward pass's argmax caches are the credit-routing table for an exact, multiply-free backward sweep}{figure.1}{}}
\newlabel{sec:substrate}{{3}{3}{}{section.3}{}}
\newlabel{fig:gatelaw}{{2}{3}{The gate law. A $z$-scored gate (red) fires at a fixed quantile regardless of regime---stationary and shifted streams are indistinguishable at every threshold---because self-normalization erases regime information. The two-timescale absolute-margin gate (blue) separates the regimes by construction: it self-quiets on stationary data (dashed, $10^{-2}$ to $10^{-4}$) while storming at shifts}{figure.2}{}}
\newlabel{sec:gate}{{4}{3}{}{section.4}{}}
\newlabel{tab:ladder}{{1}{4}{The ladder. Every gate pre-registered pass/kill criteria before its run. HC = headroom captured $=1-R_{\mathrm {oracle}}/R^{\mathrm {frozen}}_{\mathrm {oracle}}$}{table.1}{}}
\newlabel{sec:ladder}{{5}{4}{}{section.5}{}}
\newlabel{sec:pareto}{{5.2}{4}{}{subsection.5.2}{}}
\newlabel{fig:pareto}{{3}{4}{Quality vs.\ update compute on identical streams. No incumbent cell is below-and-left of ours; the cheapest cell beating our quality (LoRA, drift-triggered) pays $3.3\times $ our update budget and a $2.7\times $ activation-memory class. GPUs keep the unconstrained-compute end}{figure.3}{}}
\newlabel{sec:life}{{5.3}{4}{}{subsection.5.3}{}}
\newlabel{sec:negatives}{{5.4}{4}{}{subsection.5.4}{}}
\citation{espeholt2018impala,horgan2018distributed}
\citation{elsayed2024streaming}
\citation{sutton1991dyna}
\newlabel{fig:life}{{4}{5}{One process, 10M tokens, five rotated domain cycles. Top: prequential CE of the live learner vs.\ its frozen twin. Bottom: gate fire rate; kicks collapse $1{,}275\to 45$ per cycle; two late eras are fully silent and 42 of cycle 5's 45 kicks land in one storm at the final code revisit---the device learned its world, then mostly just served}{figure.4}{}}
\newlabel{fig:retention}{{5}{5}{Goal B. Top: held-out probe CE per domain at every era boundary; after the first cycle the trade is stable and improves with revisits (bounded, non-increasing interference). Bottom: weight norm reaches equilibrium ($+2.3\%$ over the life; slope decelerates $12\times $)}{figure.5}{}}
